<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103844" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλωπός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤψ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seen from afar, far away</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλωπὸς οἰχνεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					564
				</span></i>
			; without context in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				2.359
			</span></i> (Gomphi, Hymn to lsis), Lyr. in <i>Mitt. a. d.
				Papyrussamml. der Nationalbibliothek in Wien</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				1932
			</span></i>)<i><span class="en">
				p.139
			</span></i>; fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλῶπις</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				900
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				1188
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> restored <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήλιστον</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. of sound,
				<i>heard from afar</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰωά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					216
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλεφανής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
